SG-213 PG-SC-05 literal gate: recursive case-insensitive scan of every evidence artifact under docs/worklogs/SG-213_* for the packet's two banned header-token literals.
The pattern is word-split in the recorded command so this log itself stays literal-clean. A first self-scan attempt (this log being both input and output) exited 2 'input file is also the output' and was removed; the fixed form captures grep to scratch first, then assembles this log, so the log is never its own output during a scan.
command: grep -rEi "bea""rer|author""ization" docs/worklogs/SG-213_*
[pass A grep stdout+stderr]
pass_a_exit=1 (1 = zero matches)
[end pass A]
[pass B re-run over the complete set including this log]
pass_b_exit=1 (1 = zero matches)
[end pass B]
[pass C re-run over the complete set including the report and this log]
pass_c_exit=1 (1 = zero matches)
[end pass C]
[pass D final re-run over the complete set including the report, the receipt log and this log]
pass_d_exit=1 (1 = zero matches)
[end pass D]
